.TH KTX_VALIDATE 1 "2026-10-27" "ktx (Rust port)" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ktx_validate \- validate a KTX2 file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ktx
validate [OPTION...] <input\-file>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Checks a KTX2 file against the KTX 2.0 specification and prints the errors and warnings
found. The exit status is non\-zero when the file is invalid.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-format <format>
text, json or mini\-json.
.TP
.B \-e, \-\-warnings\-as\-errors
Treat warnings as errors.
.TP
.B \-g, \-\-gltf\-basisu
Also check the KHR_texture_basisu glTF requirements.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
ktx validate tex.ktx2
.fi
.SH NOTES
This is an unofficial Rust port of Khronos KTX\-Software (libktx and the ktx CLI); it is not
the Khronos build of the tool. The complete, current option list is printed by
.B ktx validate \-\-help.
.SH SEE ALSO
ktx(1)
